        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Dog breeds: Yorkshire Terrier, Cavalier King Charles Spaniel, Chihuahua, Papillon, Pointer\n- Organizations: The Kennel Club, American Kennel Club\n- Medical conditions: Hypoplasia of dens\n- Places: Yorkshire, England\n\nFacts:\n- The Yorkshire Terrier was developed during the 19th century in Yorkshire, England.\n- The Yorkshire Terrier is a small terrier-type dog breed that was developed to catch rats in clothing mills.\n- The Cavalier King Charles Spaniel is a small spaniel classified as a toy dog by The Kennel Club and the American Kennel Club.\n- Hypoplasia of dens is more commonly seen in the Chihuahua, the Papillon, the Pointer, and the Yorkshire Terrier.",
